    "coefficient": {
      "word": "COEFFICIENT",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Coöperating; acting together to produce an effect. Co`ef*fi\"cient*ly, adv.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "That which unites in action with something else to produce the same effect.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Etym: [Cf. F. coefficient.] (Math.)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A number or letter put before a letter or quantity, known or unknown, to show how many times the latter is to be taken; as, 6x; bx; here 6 and b are coefficients of x.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Physics)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A number, commonly used in computation as a factor, expressing the amount of some change or effect under certain fixed conditions as to temperature, length, volume, etc.; as, the coefficient of expansion; the coefficient of friction. Arbitrary coefficient (Math.), a literal coefficient placed arbitrarily in an algebraic, expression, the value of the coefficient being afterwards determined by the conditions of the problem.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
